&lt;p&gt;Astranis is a fast-growing company where hardware, software, and operations teams ship on a tight schedule. The tools to work faster, especially AI tools, are already here. What we need now is someone to help every team use them well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our AI Enablement &amp;amp; Learning and Development Lead, you will own how Astranis learns. For your first three quarters, your focus is AI enablement: getting real, measurable adoption of the tools we already have. From there, you will broaden into a full learning and development function, including team-level onboarding, on-demand skills training, and a manager academy. You will be a hands-on individual contributor who designs, builds, and runs programs yourself, with room to grow the function and, over time, scale into a leadership role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Director of Employee Success and sit on our AI Steering Committee.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Execute on our AI Enablement Strategy (this is the focus for the first three quarters)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 Pillars to this strategy:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn our existing AI training content (101 through 103) into a polished, formal curriculum with clear learning paths for different roles and skill levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and launch an AI for Managers course that gets team leads using these tools themselves and coaching their teams to do the same.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate company-wide hackathons twice a year, owning logistics, communications, judging, and follow-through so winning ideas turn into real workflow improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate our superuser community. Our best AI practitioners are already spread across the company and active in Slack; your job is to showcase their work through lunch and learns, workshops, and internal spotlights, and to make it easy for others to learn from them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor key metrics like weekly average logins by team to evaluate progress and identify hotspots.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide feedback to the AI Steering Committee, bringing usage data and employee feedback to inform decisions on tools and policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Formalize our learning and development function&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with team leads to identify skill gaps and design team-level onboarding that gets new hires productive faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create targeted training on demand where teams need more support. (For example, a proposal writing workshop for teams responding to customer RFPs.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and launch a leadership academy program scoped for director-level leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish simple, repeatable ways to measure whether training works, and use what you learn to improve every program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create lightweight systems, templates, and a knowledge base so learning scales beyond live sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a framework to assess the feasibility and business case for an engineering rotational program, define program requirements and structure, and lead the design, development, and implementation of the program if approved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in learning and development, enablement, change management, or internal training, ideally at a fast-growing technology or engineering company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of running adoption or enablement programs end to end and being able to show the results with data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on fluency with AI tools. You use them regularly and can teach others to use them well, from complete beginners to power users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong instructional design and facilitation skills, in live workshops and in self-serve formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or running internal communities, events, or hackathons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort earning trust with highly technical employees and managers who are very busy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise communication and the ability to work independently, prioritize across many requests, and move quickly with limited process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching a manager or leadership development program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background supporting engineering, aerospace, or other deeply technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with learning platforms or LMS tools, and with analytics for tracking usage and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with executives or a steering committee on technology rollouts.&lt;/li&gt;
